<title>USA: LVMH and Miller break off talks.</title>
<headline>LVMH and Miller break off talks.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>LVMH Moet Hennessy Louis Vuitton, the Paris-based luxury products group, said Wednesday it will not pursue negotiations with Robert Miller for the acquisition of his 38.75 percent interest in DFS, of which the LVMH group owns the remaining 61.25 percent.</p>
<p>As a result, said the company, LVMH and Miller will together continue as shareholders of DFS, the world's largest distributor of luxury goods, whose principal outlets are in the Asia-Pacific region.</p>
</text>
